00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.000
Or how LangFuse basically caches your prompts.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.000
What was the benefit of this?

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:05.000
The benefit was that whenever you are using your rag application,

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.000
okay?

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.000
Whenever you are invoking this application,

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.000
then in the augmentation step,

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.000
you need your system prompt,

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:13.000
then here again and again,

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:16.000
you are not pulling this particular prompt

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.000
by calling API on the servers of LangFuse.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.000
Because every time you are calling API,

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.000
and each of the requests,

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:26.000
then it is adding unnecessary latency.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.000
So what is the fix of LangFuse?

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:33.000
The fix of LangFuse is that you maintain a local cache.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.000
And in this local cache,

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.000
you save your prompt,

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:40.000
whether it is a system prompt or any other type of prompt,

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.000
you save this prompt in your local cache.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.000
And this cache refresh or update work,

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:51.000
it will automatically handle in the background of LangFuse.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.000
So what is the flow?

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:57.000
The flow is that your application always pulls the prompts

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:00.000
from a local database.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.000
Whereas LangFuse handles the work of updating this database in the background.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.000
And at the end of LangFuse,

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.000
two databases work here.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:11.000
The first is your primary database,

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.000
which is your Redis database,

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.000
which acts as a cache.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:18.000
And this connects to your permanent database,

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.000
that is your PostgreSQL database.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:24.000
So here your permanent database is also connected.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.000
I hope you remember all this flow.

